1. sá, prs. that, sts. weakened to an article, 🞄the (only nm. n. sá, f. sā́, and in RV. lc. 🞄sasmin;
 the s of the nm. m. is always dropped 🞄before consonants except once in RV. before 🞄p and once before t;
 sa sts. coalesces with a 🞄following vowel);
